== Maiden ==
=== Draining and Bow Flicking ===
Maiden has a chance to drain the combat stats of your highest attack bonus. Bow flicking (not necessarily a bow) is when you swap to a different style so that maiden drains a different stat instead of your melee stats. Since Maiden attacks on a 10-tick cycle this is as simple as equipping your ranged weapon after every 2 scythe swings then re-equipping your scythe as soon as Maidens attack animation begins.

The minimum swaps required will depend on your gear, but some common swaps are listed below:

<u>Blood fury:</u>
Single way Twisted Bow | 
Single way ZCB | 
Single way Black chinchompa | 
Single way Tonalztics of Ralos

<u>Rancour:</u>
Twisted Bow + Anguish | 
Twisted Bow + Salve amulet (e) |
Single way ZCB |
Black chinchompa + Buckler |
Twisted Bow + Void gloves |
Single way Tonalztics of Ralos

Additional notes:
You should always repot with a regular super combat if you ever get drained at maiden. 
When ranging in 4s you should repot a ranged dose before chinning if you have been drained.
When ranging in 5s you should be south of maiden to avoid getting drained excessively before chinning 50s.

=== Stacking and Cross Freezing ===
==== Stacking ====
Stacking is when we freeze the 50s nylos on top of the old 70s nylos, then kill them all together. We do this by staying on boss as the freezers deal with 70s, often using ZCB/claw/DPS specs to push the 50s proc. We deal damage to the various 70s/50s with a Dinh's Bulwark and let freezers freeze the clump to death. 

Dinh's Bulwark has a special attack, Shield Bash, which hits up to 10 enemies in an 11×11 area around the player. This is one of the most efficient methods for quickly damaging crabs when stacking to prevent leaks. The targeted NPC is hit twice by the attack, while all other monsters are hit once. When using Dinh's special attack, it is important to target the newest or highest HP crab in the stack to maximize the double hit. This is usually the second crab in the stack. MAKE SURE YOUR DINHS IS NOT ON DEFENSIVE.

==== Crossfreezing ====
This method of freezing is better than normal freezing when stacking. Both magers need to change their playstyle for this method, so make sure to confirm with your other mager before entering the raid that you want to crossfreeze.

Typically, NFRZ takes N1234 and SFRZ takes S12. Instead, both magers will now swap who freezes N1 and S1:

* Nfrz will first freeze S1 1st tick, then N234.
* Sfrz will freeze N1 1 tick after it spawns, then S2 into the clump.

Why is this better?
The N1 being frozen 1 tick later allows it to be within range of the dinh's spec that happens on N2. This is why it's important for N1 to be frozen 1 tick late by the SFRZ.
Make sure to crossfreeze all spawns during maiden to keep it consistent.

In 4s, there may not be a S1 and/or N1 spawn, in which case the following applies.

NFRZ if no S1 to freeze:
* On 70s: Freeze maiden
* NFRZ On 50s and 30s: Freeze the clump

SFRZ if no N1 to freeze:
* On 70s: Insta-freeze N2
* NFRZ On 50s and 30s: Freeze the clump

=== Ice Rush ===
Usually performed in lower scales and/or solo freeze scenarios. The mager instantly Ice Rushes S2 while DPS roles scythe/claw spec N1 and/or S1, then proceeds to Ice Barrage N234 as normal. This lets S2 join the clump because of shorter freeze duration when 4s get frozen.

=== SBS freezing ===
Very difficult I'm not even gonna try explaining here. Requires SBS and manual-cast freezing in the same tick, repeatedly. If SFRZ, you can 'preload' SBS to catch S1 easily and just try to get S2. NFRZ must be tick-perfect on all crabs as usual. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DTzzl1QTh9E

== Bloat ==
=== Pre-Firing ===
Allows you to hit bloat with a ranged/magic weapon while he is walking before he downs
You get 3 risk-free pre-fires (no chance of turning) at the start of the room. Every pre-fire after you risk turning (unless you know the down mechanics very well but there are feet falling so riskier.) 
Low reward for looking extremely frickin cool.

=== Flinches === 
Allow you to chally after avoiding the bloat stomp. Always guarantees at least 1 fly. If everyone challys, 1 fly per person and it bounces.

=== Phoenix Necklace Usage (PNecking) ===
SBS/Humidify and Phoenix Necklaces are used in conjunction to stall fly damage and consequentially proc Phoenix Necklace to both
regenerate health and void other flies while hitting Bloat. This is often used to try to get 1-downs in normal TOB for speed times. 
The role generally falls under MDPS due to their higher inventory space. Not generally used for regular raids.

